# Phase 10 Task 18: the root and health route group.
#
# Import this file inside the site's route block. Argument 0 is the one
# upstream that serves GET /, GET /health, GET /health/live and
# GET /health/ready. There is no second argument and no fallback in this
# snippet: the group has exactly one owner at a time.
#
# The matcher names the four paths exactly and no method, so a wrong method
# reaches the same owner and gets its shared 405. A trailing slash or a
# longer path is not named here and stays with the site's own fallback.
#
# Rollback is one change: remove the single import line.
#
# The transport settings have no passive health (fail_duration, max_fails).
# The group has a single upstream and no fallback, so a remembered failure
# would leave nothing to select until it expired, and the group would keep
# answering 503 after its upstream was back. A refused connection is a
# dial error before any request bytes are sent, so it is retried every
# lb_try_interval until lb_try_duration ends, which bridges a restart.
#
# The installed Caddy file is a separate review; this file is source only.
(verdaxis_rust_root_health) {
	@root_health path / /health /health/live /health/ready
	handle @root_health {
		reverse_proxy {args[0]} {
			lb_policy first
			lb_try_duration 10s
			lb_try_interval 250ms
			flush_interval -1
			transport http {
				keepalive off
			}
		}
	}
}
